    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nI'm using neovim on Arch Linux with a plugin called [`vimtex`](https://github.com/lervag/vimtex).\nOn neovim 0.12.2 using `:lua vim.pack.update()` works fine, but on neovim 0.12.3 running the same command tries to downgrade vimtex from `2.17` to `2.7.1`.\n\nRunning `git bisect` returns dd95e434e39876b92ff61969b0d7f38e994800fb as the problematic commit.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRun neovim with the following config:\n\n```lua\nvim.pack.add({\n\t{\n\t\tsrc = \"https://github.com/lervag/vimtex\",\n\t\tversion = vim.version.range(\"*\"),\n\t},\n})\n```\n\nand see it it tries to install `vimtex` version `2.7.1` (wrong) or `2.17` (correct).\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nInstall `vimtex` version `2.17` as it is semantically the higher version.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.12.3\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\ndid not try as vim does not have `vim.pack`\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArch Linux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.47.4\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from source and `git bisect`",
